From f0750c226b13715c7513becc3686e1ec0ee70353 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Per Jonsson <pertyjons@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:37:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add an amplifier, and let the diff answer the fourth gate
 bullet
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ADR-0004 clause 2 says the fourth Phase 2 gate is decided by a change
rather than by an opinion: adding a second simple DSP node must touch no
line of the renderer's control flow, and the check is performed by making
that change. This is that change.

The amplifier is the first node with two inputs and two signal domains —
audio scaled sample by sample by a control — so it also exercises the
port table's domain rule with a node that has a domain to get wrong.
Either input unpatched makes it silent, which is the same rule as
everywhere else in this crate rather than an invented level.

The diff touches the IR vocabulary, the registry, a kernel, and a test.
It touches no line of `render/hot.rs`, and none of the compiler, the
validator, the arena, or the report either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
